"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwaypower_docs=self.webpackChunkwaypower_docs||[]).push([["2062"],{5839(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"building-these-docs-with-waypower","metadata":{"permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/building-these-docs-with-waypower","editUrl":"https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116/waypower-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-09-23-building-these-docs-with-waypower.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-09-23-building-these-docs-with-waypower.md","title":"This site was built by the skills it documents","description":"The fastest way to find out whether a workflow pack works is to make it build","date":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"dogfooding","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/tags/dogfooding"},{"inline":true,"label":"meta","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/tags/meta"},{"inline":true,"label":"waypower","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/tags/waypower"}],"readingTime":2.78,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Mohamed Eslam","title":"waypower maintainer","url":"https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116","imageURL":"https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116.png","key":"mohmaedeslam","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"building-these-docs-with-waypower","title":"This site was built by the skills it documents","authors":"mohmaedeslam","tags":["dogfooding","meta","waypower"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"waypower v0.1.0: 13 skills, one pipeline","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/waypower-v0-1-0"}},"content":"The fastest way to find out whether a workflow pack works is to make it build\\r\\nits own marketing site. So that\'s what we did: the pages you\'re reading were\\r\\ndesigned, planned, and shipped through the waypower pipeline itself. This is\\r\\nthe honest log of what that looked like.\\r\\n\\r\\n{/* truncate */}\\r\\n\\r\\n## The request was one sentence\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Build a docs site for the pack. New repo, a popular docs template, and use\\r\\nour own skills to do it.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nA vague brief \u2014 which is exactly the trigger condition for\\r\\n[`design-interview`](/docs/skills/design-interview). It fired, and instead of\\r\\nscaffolding immediately, the agent asked. Two rounds:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **Register, users, purpose, outcome.** Inferred hypotheses from the\\r\\n   waypower repo (developers evaluating the pack in under five minutes; the\\r\\n   install command as the success metric), confirmed and sharpened in\\r\\n   conversation.\\r\\n2. **Brand personality.** Four candidate personalities; the pick was\\r\\n   *confident engineering* \u2014 \\"Stripe/Vercel docs: the certainty of an expert\\r\\n   who doesn\'t need noise.\\" Plus the explicit anti-reference: AI-hype landing\\r\\n   pages with gradient blobs and empty promises.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe interview also settled the one architectural decision: **Docusaurus** \u2014\\r\\nchosen for its built-in blog (this post needed somewhere to live), versioning\\r\\nthat will track pack releases, and first-class GitHub Pages deployment.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The spec became artifacts before it became code\\r\\n\\r\\nThe interview\'s output was committed to the repo *before* any page existed:\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`PRODUCT.md`** \u2014 who the site serves, what success looks like, the five\\r\\n  design principles (\\"show, don\'t tell\\", \\"the install command is sacred\\",\\r\\n  \\"answer-first pages\\", \\"calm authority\\", \\"practice what you preach\\").\\r\\n- **`DESIGN.md`** \u2014 the seeded visual system: a pure-white surface, one deep\\r\\n  marine-teal primary (seeded at OKLCH hue 200\xb0) doing all the brand work, a\\r\\n  saturated amber accent rationed to badges and the primary CTA, Inter +\\r\\n  JetBrains Mono, near-zero motion.\\r\\n\\r\\nEvery color on this site traces back to that file. The \\"no shadows, 1px\\r\\nborders\\" rule is why nothing here glows.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Then the pipeline did what it does\\r\\n\\r\\n- **Planning:** the build was sliced into verifiable tickets \u2014 config, theme,\\r\\n  content, landing, blog, deploy \u2014 each shippable on its own.\\r\\n- **Verification ([completion-gate](/docs/skills/completion-gate)):** \\"the\\r\\n  site works\\" was not accepted until `docusaurus build` ran green and every\\r\\n  internal link resolved \u2014 evidence, not assertion.\\r\\n- **Ship ([finish-handoff](/docs/skills/finish-handoff)):** clean git history,\\r\\n  pushed to a dedicated public repo, deployed to GitHub Pages, and this\\r\\n  handoff of a blog post so the next session starts warm.\\r\\n\\r\\n## What dogfooding actually surfaced\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo honest observations:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. **The interview gate paid for itself immediately.** The template question\\r\\n   alone (Docusaurus vs VitePress vs Starlight vs MkDocs Material) would have\\r\\n   been a coin flip without the interview\'s criteria: blog + versioning +\\r\\n   Pages deploy made it a one-minute decision.\\r\\n2. **The pipeline bends for content work.** Strict RED-GREEN TDD doesn\'t map\\r\\n   onto prose. The skills adapted \u2014 verification became \\"build passes, links\\r\\n   resolve\\" \u2014 which is exactly what a good process should do: hold the\\r\\n   discipline, flex the mechanics.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The takeaway\\r\\n\\r\\nA workflow you wouldn\'t use on your own project is a workflow you shouldn\'t\\r\\nship. This site is the proof artifact: the same pipeline documented in the\\r\\n[skills reference](/docs/skills/using-waypower) produced the design system,\\r\\nthe content, and the deploy \u2014 in one session, with the gates doing their job.\\r\\n\\r\\nTry it on yours:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nnpx skills add mohmaedeslam00116/waypower --all -g --copy\\r\\n```"},{"id":"waypower-v0-1-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/waypower-v0-1-0","editUrl":"https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116/waypower-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-09-23-waypower-v0-1-0.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-09-23-waypower-v0-1-0.md","title":"waypower v0.1.0: 13 skills, one pipeline","description":"Your agent already knows how to code. The bottleneck was never the model\'s","date":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"waypower","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/tags/waypower"}],"readingTime":1.37,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Mohamed Eslam","title":"waypower maintainer","url":"https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116","imageURL":"https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116.png","key":"mohmaedeslam","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"waypower-v0-1-0","title":"waypower v0.1.0: 13 skills, one pipeline","authors":"mohmaedeslam","tags":["release","waypower"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"This site was built by the skills it documents","permalink":"/waypower-docs/blog/building-these-docs-with-waypower"}},"content":"Your agent already knows how to code. The bottleneck was never the model\'s\\r\\nsyntax \u2014 it\'s that nobody taught it *how to work*: how to refuse a vague\\r\\nbrief, how to plan before building, how to prove a claim before making it.\\r\\n\\r\\nwaypower v0.1.0 is out today: **13 pressure-tested agent skills** forming one\\r\\nidea-to-ship pipeline for Claude Code and compatible harnesses.\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nnpx skills add mohmaedeslam00116/waypower --all -g --copy\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n{/* truncate */}\\r\\n\\r\\n## What\'s in the pack\\r\\n\\r\\n- **1 orchestrator** \u2014 `using-waypower`, always active, routes every task to\\r\\n  the right process skill and disarms the rationalizations agents use to skip\\r\\n  process.\\r\\n- **8 process skills** \u2014 auto-invoked on their triggers: `design-interview`,\\r\\n  `tracer-plan`, `seam-design`, `seam-driven-tdd`, `hypothesis-debugging`,\\r\\n  `domain-glossary`, `completion-gate`, `dual-axis-review`.\\r\\n- **4 tool skills** \u2014 invoked by name when you want them: `waymap`,\\r\\n  `finish-handoff`, `deep-research`, `authoring-skills`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Why \\"pressure-tested\\" is on the label\\r\\n\\r\\nEvery skill was graded against paired baseline runs \u2014 the same pressure\\r\\nscenario executed with and without the skill. **12 of 13 discriminate\\r\\ncleanly**: agents with the skill demonstrably behave differently than agents\\r\\nwithout it. The thirteenth (`domain-glossary`) is documented honestly and\\r\\nbeing hardened for the next release.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe eval scenarios ship inside the pack (`evals/evals.json` per skill), so you\\r\\ncan re-run the evidence yourself instead of taking our word for it.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Where to go\\r\\n\\r\\n- [Getting started](/docs/getting-started) \u2014 five minutes to your first\\r\\n  pipeline session\\r\\n- [The pipeline](/docs/pipeline) \u2014 the six stages and where you stay in the\\r\\n  loop\\r\\n- [Skills reference](/docs/skills/using-waypower) \u2014 all 13 in detail\\r\\n- [GitHub](https://github.com/mohmaedeslam00116/waypower) \xb7\\r\\n  [skills.sh](https://skills.sh/mohmaedeslam00116/waypower)"}]}}')}}]);